"""Further source-reviewed mainland Hoenn terminal service and civilian speech."""
ROWS = []
def add(key, labels, subject, lines):
    replies = [line.strip() for line in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies) == 11, (key, len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='hoenn_service_' + key, labels=labels.split(), subject=subject, replies=replies))

add('trend_indispensable','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_CantImagineLifeWithoutTrend','A girl says she cannot imagine life without the current trend.','''laughing~The trend has become essential equipment for being alive. That escalated quickly.|A strong attachment, though fashionable interests do tend to change.|Enjoy it. Keep room for other things too.|It must have made her days more interesting.|A favorite thing can add a lot of flavor to ordinary days.|The newest fashion has been promoted to a fundamental condition of existence.|I suspect life will somehow continue when the next trend arrives.|That is a very ambitious claim for something recently fashionable.|A new delight can feel as though it was always missing.|A favorite trend can feel like it has always belonged.|I wonder what first made it so important to her.''')
add('trend_bored','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_GettingBoredOfTrend','A girl is getting bored of the current trend and wants the next one.','''soft_smile~The trend has worn out its welcome. Next excitement, please form a line.|Novelty fading is a familiar pattern in rapidly shared interests.|No need to force it. Find what you actually enjoy.|It is all right for a favorite thing to stop fitting.|Sometimes a familiar flavor just needs a little time away.|The reigning sensation has received notice of its impending replacement.|An entire era has ended at the first hint of boredom.|I wonder whether changing how she enjoys it would help.|Not every little delight needs to stay forever.|A trend can have a good run without becoming a lifetime commitment.|I would ask what she hopes the next big thing will offer.''')
add('trend_teaching_partner','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_TeachingMonAboutTrend','A woman realizes teaching her Pokemon about the trend may be too much.','''soft_smile~Her Pokemon may have its own hobbies. Possibly staring at something tiny.|The subject may not be relevant to the Pokemon's own interests.|Let the partner choose what catches its attention.|I know that feeling when nobody understands your favorite thing.|Sharing is nice. Insisting can spoil the fun for both.|A devoted teacher has met a student with a completely different syllabus.|The Pokemon has declined to become fashionable on command.|A different approach might help, if the learner is interested at all.|Affection need not mean loving every same little thing.|Her partner is allowed a taste that skips the current trend.|I would watch what the Pokemon tries to show her in return.''')
add('trend_hunch_yes','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_MyHunchWasRight','An older man celebrates confirmation that his guess about a trend was right.','''laughing~One step closer to hip! Careful, it might be a slippery floor.|A confirmed hunch can make learning unfamiliar fashions rather encouraging.|Good guess. No need to race everyone else.|He sounds so pleased. That is rather lovely.|A little encouragement can make joining in feel easier.|Our enthusiastic scholar of fashion has acquired supporting testimony.|Hip and happening has apparently admitted one more applicant.|A small successful prediction is a good reason to keep asking questions.|A little certainty has brightened his whole afternoon.|Confidence looks good on someone willing to learn.|I like that he is still curious about what other people enjoy.''')
add('trend_hunch_no','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_NotEasyToKeepUp','An older man admits difficulty keeping up after his trend guess is rejected.','''soft_smile~The trend ran ahead of him. That does not mean he has to sprint.|Changing fashions are difficult to track without clear definitions.|He can ask. Nothing wrong with not knowing.|I hope he does not feel silly for trying.|It is nice that he wanted to join the conversation at all.|A failed guess need not end our brave explorer's cultural expedition.|Keeping up is exhausting when the destination keeps wandering.|A few questions are cheaper than pretending to understand.|He can enjoy the company without mastering every new phrase.|Nobody stays current on everything, especially at this speed.|I would rather meet someone curious than someone afraid to ask.''')
add('trend_tv','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_TVShowAboutTrend','A man wonders whether the current trend has its own TV show.','''soft_smile~It might! At this rate, the trend probably has a lunch appointment too.|A popular subject could plausibly attract a program of its own.|Worth checking the listings. No need to guess.|He might find other people enjoying the same thing there.|A show can be a nice excuse to gather and talk.|The trend is one broadcast away from achieving complete household occupation.|If it has a theme song, this town may never recover.|I wonder what a whole program would actually demonstrate.|Shared interests often seek a little place to gather.|A television special would certainly make the trend feel established.|I would ask whether he remembers seeing an episode or just hearing about it.''')
add('trend_overseas','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_IsTrendMorePopularAcrossSea','A twin wonders whether the trend is even more popular overseas.','''surprised~Maybe the trend sailed first and forgot to send us a postcard.|Comparing places could reveal whether this is local or widespread.|Only way to know is ask someone who has been there.|I like wondering what people elsewhere are talking about.|Some favorites travel well. Others stay a hometown specialty.|Our little island's obsession may have developed an international itinerary.|The question is whether the rest of the world caught this particular fever.|We would need a few visitors' reports before making a useful map.|The sea separates places without stopping every shared idea.|A trend can look rather different once it reaches another crowd.|That would be a fun question to ask the next traveler.''')
add('trend_collector','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_CollectTrendMerchandise','A boy lists licensed trend merchandise then refuses to share it.','''laughing~Dolls, clothes, books, and a very sturdy fence around sharing.|A comprehensive collection, with unusually emphatic ownership rules.|His things, his choice. No need to grab.|I was only going to look. He sounded ready for a siege.|He can keep his collection. I hope he enjoys it.|A guided tour of the collection, followed by an immediate closure to visitors.|The licensing is official. So is the hostility toward borrowing.|That is a lot of matching equipment for one interest.|A favorite collection can feel like a small private world.|A coordinated collection with absolutely no lending policy.|I would ask which piece is his favorite, from a respectful distance.''')
add('trend_authentic','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_AllegedTrendNotAuthentic','A debater rejects an alleged trend sighting with vague claims about authenticity.','''laughing~Sharper AND more mellow? My understanding has developed a small wobble.|Those criteria need definitions before we can verify the distinction.|Hard to compare anything with that explanation.|I am not sure I know more than I did before.|A strong opinion needs something clearer than an impressive description.|A masterclass in certainty conducted without any usable evidence.|The authentic article has escaped description with remarkable confidence.|I would need measurable differences before rebuilding my opinion.|Sometimes the claim to know is louder than the knowledge.|Authenticity usually benefits from more than a grand hand gesture.|I would love to see both examples side by side.''')
add('trend_singing','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_WorkOnYourSinging','A debater tells a trend enthusiast to improve their singing first.','''flustered~A gentler music review might have used fewer elbows.|Practical feedback would help more than a dismissive verdict.|Could have said that more kindly.|Practice helps. So does not making someone ashamed to try.|A little encouragement would make that advice easier to take.|A critique has arrived with all its edges left unnecessarily sharp.|Apparently we have entered the compulsory humiliation portion of singing.|Specific advice would give the singer something useful to change.|A voice can grow more easily when it is not afraid.|Honest feedback does not require an unflattering delivery.|I would rather hear what the singer enjoys about their song.''')
add('trend_party','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_BrilliantIndeed','A debater enthusiastically agrees to a trend party to settle who is best.','''laughing~A party to determine the champion of a trend. Will there be tiny medals?|A friendly gathering could be enjoyable if the contest stays friendly.|Have the party. Skip making it a grudge.|I hope they enjoy being together more than winning.|A party needs snacks before it needs a reigning champion.|A social occasion has been promoted into the axis of their entire lives.|Their enthusiasm has annexed the calendar with alarming speed.|First decide what being the best actually means.|A shared joy need not divide people into winners.|A themed party sounds lovely if everyone leaves room for each other.|I would be curious who they invite to judge this very serious event.''')
add('trend_professor','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_TrendWeighsHeavilyOnMind','A debater calls an enthusiast a professor because the trend fills their thoughts.','''laughing~A whole professorship for thinking about it constantly. I might qualify in snacks.|Enthusiasm is not quite the same as expertise, though it can encourage study.|Sounds like they need a break from thinking about it.|I know what it is like when an idea will not leave.|A favorite thing should still leave room for sleep and supper.|An honorary title has been awarded for extraordinary mental occupation.|The institution has very flexible standards for awarding a chair.|A rest might make the next idea clearer, professor or otherwise.|Something can matter deeply without filling every quiet hour.|Devotion is charming until it becomes the only thing one wears.|I would ask what first made the subject catch their imagination.''')
add('trend_duo','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_WellBeTrendDuo','Two trend enthusiasts agree to team up as a named duo.','''soft_smile~A duo! Twice the enthusiasm, approximately the same number of doubts.|Collaboration may bring more ideas than either would find alone.|Good. Work together instead of arguing.|They sound pleased to have found someone who understands.|A shared project is often more fun than doing it alone.|The partnership has acquired a name and an impressive opening laugh.|Two minds, one obsession. I wish the neighbors patience.|A second perspective can improve even a very enthusiastic plan.|Finding someone who shares your delight can feel like luck.|Every good duo needs room for both personalities.|I would like to see what they decide to do together first.''')
add('trend_sludge','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_LoveSludgeBombButTrendInToo','A fan of Sludge Bomb acknowledges another move is currently fashionable.','''laughing~Sludge Bomb is still their favorite. Fashion has not washed that away.|Personal preference and current popularity can coexist quite comfortably.|Use what works for the partner, trend or not.|I like that they have kept their own favorite.|A popular choice does not have to replace a familiar one.|The old favorite has graciously admitted a fashionable rival to the conversation.|They have a loyal heart and an unusually muddy taste.|Worth considering the move itself before following the popularity chart.|A favorite need not disappear when other people admire something new.|Knowing the trend and keeping your own taste can work beautifully.|I would ask what made Sludge Bomb their favorite in the first place.''')

add('daycare_intro','Route117_Text_SeeWifeIfYoudLikeMeToRaiseMon','The Day-Care Man introduces the service and directs enrollment to his wife.','''soft_smile~He handles the welcome; his wife handles the important arranging bits.|A clear division of responsibilities. We know whom to ask.|Talk to his wife if we need the help.|It is good to know who would be looking after them.|Entrusting a partner to someone deserves a proper conversation.|Our introduction comes with an admirably direct referral.|A rare introduction that tells us exactly who can actually help.|A little clarity about how the place works is useful.|Care begins with knowing whose hands we are trusting.|A polite welcome with a very practical next step.|I would ask them how an ordinary day here goes.''')
add('daycare_egg_space','Route117_Text_YouHaveNoRoomForIt','The Day-Care Man cannot hand over an Egg until the players party has room.','''soft_smile~A new little possibility needs a proper place, not a balancing act.|We need space in the party before accepting responsibility for the Egg.|Make room first. The Egg stays safe here.|I would want to be ready before taking it.|Something so delicate deserves a careful welcome.|Our new arrival must wait while its traveling arrangements are made.|The Egg has very sensibly declined to become excess baggage.|Capacity matters when the next passenger needs gentle handling.|Let it wait safely until we can carry it with care.|A thoughtful arrival begins with making an actual place.|I would check our arrangements before asking for it again.''')
add('daycare_decline','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_FineThenComeAgain','The Day-Care Woman accepts declining the initial care offer.','''soft_smile~No stay today. It is nice to leave with the invitation still open.|We can return if the arrangement suits us later.|Not needed today. Good to know they are here.|That was an easy, kind way to accept the answer.|We can keep our partner close and visit another time.|The proposed stay has been declined without any awkward curtain call.|An ordinary no, received with refreshing efficiency.|No change needed when the present arrangement is working.|The offer can remain kind without being accepted.|A pleasant exit makes a return visit much easier.|She sounded happy to let us choose our own timing.''')
add('daycare_end','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_ComeAgain','The Day-Care Woman closes a canceled or completed service conversation.','''soft_smile~All settled for now. We can head on and visit again later.|The arrangement is finished for the moment. A clear stopping point.|We are done here. Thank her before we go.|A simple goodbye after all the arranging.|It is good to leave knowing where we stand.|The business of the visit concludes with a modest farewell.|A pleasingly brief ending to an occasionally complicated errand.|Everything needed for this visit seems to be settled.|A familiar goodbye can keep a place welcoming.|A neat little close to the conversation.|I would be glad to return to such a straightforward welcome.''')
add('daycare_one','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_YouHaveJustOneMon','The Day-Care Woman refuses to take the players only Pokemon.','''soft_smile~We should keep our traveling friend with us. That is a fair rule.|Leaving the only partner would remove our ability to battle safely.|Keep our partner. We need each other out there.|I would feel very exposed heading out alone.|Their care includes making sure we can manage the trip.|Our sole traveling companion has been correctly kept on the guest list.|The journey is rather less practical without anyone to share it.|The team needs a working minimum before we can change its members.|Some company is too important to leave behind today.|Keeping the only partner close is the sensible arrangement.|She noticed the problem before letting us create it.''')
add('daycare_last_ready','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_WhatWillYouBattleWith','The Day-Care Woman will not take the only battle-ready Pokemon.','''soft_smile~She caught the important part: someone still needs to get us home.|We would lose our last battle-ready partner. The refusal is sensible.|Heal the others first. Keep someone ready to help.|That is a reassuring thing for her to check.|A safe trip comes before any plans to leave a partner here.|The proposed arrangement has failed a very practical survival question.|Our plan briefly forgot that the road may have opinions.|Readiness matters, not just how many Pokemon are in the party.|Care for those traveling with us before changing the company.|The arrangement needs to work outside this friendly doorway too.|I appreciate that she asked the question we had overlooked.''')
add('daycare_two','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_YoullBeLeftWithJustOne','The Day-Care Woman advises obtaining more Pokemon before leaving another for care.','''soft_smile~A little backup would make the road less lonely and less risky.|A broader team offers a better margin before leaving a partner here.|Build the team a bit first. Fair advice.|I would rather leave feeling prepared than stretched thin.|One more good friendship could make the whole trip easier.|Our future planning has received a useful second opinion.|The team has not quite reached the luxury of spare company.|A little redundancy keeps a small setback from becoming a large one.|It is good to have someone beside the one carrying everything.|A fuller team leaves more room to make choices comfortably.|She is thinking about what happens after we walk out.''')
add('daycare_husband','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_HusbandWasLookingForYou','The Day-Care Woman directs the player to her husband who is looking for them.','''surprised~A message waiting outside! We should go find out what he needs.|We should speak with him rather than guessing at the reason.|Go see him. He may have something important.|I would like to know what he wanted to tell us.|Best not leave him waiting when we are already nearby.|Our quiet visit has acquired a small appointment at the front.|We have been requested. That always makes an errand sound grander.|Easy enough to check with him before we head away.|Someone has been keeping a thought for us.|A quick word with him should settle what this is about.|I would look for him before leaving the grounds.''')
add('daycare_payment','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_NotEnoughMoney','The Day-Care Woman cannot release a cared-for Pokemon without the required payment.','''sad~The care bill is more than our pockets can handle right now. We need a plan.|We should arrange the required payment before attempting collection again.|Get the fee together. Our partner is waiting.|I would want to settle this as soon as we could.|That care took time. We need to make sure we can pay for it.|The reunion has been delayed by an unfortunate lack of funds.|The bill has become the least welcome part of coming back.|We should check the full cost and make a practical plan.|The waiting makes this more than an ordinary errand now.|Time to put the necessary payment ahead of anything optional.|I would ask the exact amount and make that our next priority.''')
add('daycare_retrieve_space','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_YourTeamIsFull','The Day-Care Woman asks for party space before returning a Pokemon.','''soft_smile~Our friend needs a traveling spot before the reunion can happen.|We must make space before retrieving the Pokemon.|Make room for our partner. Then come straight back.|I would not want to keep them waiting longer than necessary.|A proper place in the team comes first.|The reunion is prepared; the travel arrangements are temporarily overbooked.|We have reached the awkward problem of too much good company.|A quick party adjustment will solve this without any fuss.|Returning deserves a place that is actually ready.|A little rearranging will make the welcome complete.|I would sort this out before taking on another errand.''')
add('interview_fan_decline','SlateportCity_PokemonFanClub_Text_HereIfYouGetUrgeToTellMe','A reporter leaves an invitation open after the player declines discussing Pokemon.','''soft_smile~No story today, but they left the door open very nicely.|A good interview should wait for a willing participant.|Talk when we want to. That works.|I appreciate not having to find the words right now.|A relaxed invitation is easier to accept another day.|The unspoken story has been granted a perfectly courteous extension.|Our silence has survived contact with a reporter. Encouraging.|No need to force information when the source is not ready.|A story can wait until its teller wants to share it.|They made a refusal feel socially quite easy.|I like that they are interested without pushing.''')
add('interview_job','SlateportCity_PokemonFanClub_Text_EnjoyDoingInterviews','A reporter enjoys learning about Pokemon through interviews.','''soft_smile~A job where people tell you about their favorite little friends. Good job.|Listening to trainers can reveal observations missed by general descriptions.|Good way to learn. Ask people who know their partners.|I like people who actually enjoy listening.|Someone else's everyday care can teach you a lot.|A fortunate profession for someone who genuinely likes other people's stories.|A living made from curiosity and the patience to let others finish.|Firsthand accounts are useful, especially when the questions are thoughtful.|Listening can be its own small kind of exploration.|People are much easier to talk to when their interest is sincere.|That is what I enjoy too: the details someone notices because they care.''')
add('museum_report_decline','SlateportCity_OceanicMuseum_1F_Text_LetMeKnowIfYouHaveStory','A reporter invites the player to return with an interesting story.','''soft_smile~We have a place to bring a good story when one finally sits still.|A standing invitation. We can return with something specific to share.|We will tell them when there is something worth telling.|It is nice not to have to be interesting on demand.|A good tale can wait until we have had time to enjoy it.|Our reporter has booked a possible future adventure without naming a date.|An excellent excuse to postpone being remarkable.|Keeping a contact for future discoveries is practical.|Some stories need to be lived before they can be spoken.|A gracious invitation that does not demand an immediate performance.|I would remember them if we came across a story worth sharing.''')
add('museum_report_done','SlateportCity_OceanicMuseum_1F_Text_BetterWriteUpStory','A reporter eagerly leaves to write a good television story.','''laughing~The story is trying to escape through their pencil. Better let them write.|Recording the details while fresh is a sound habit.|Let them work. They have what they need.|I like hearing that little spark when someone finds their idea.|A good story is ready. No sense keeping them from it.|The interview has become copy, and the deadline has found its legs.|The words must be captured before they develop other plans.|Notes now will save a lot of reconstructing details later.|A fresh thought is worth giving a little space.|They sound ready to turn the conversation into something polished.|I would like to see which detail becomes the opening.''')
add('contest_report_decline','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_PleaseDoShareStoryWithMe','A contest reporter remains interested after the player has no story to share.','''soft_smile~A little disappointed, still friendly. We can bring a better story another day.|A future account is likely more useful than one forced now.|Nothing to share yet. That is allowed.|I am glad they did not make the silence awkward.|We can wait until there is something we actually want to tell.|The hoped-for scoop has become a courteous future possibility.|Our day has escaped being turned into content for the moment.|We can keep the invitation in mind for a real discovery.|A story should arrive with a willing voice behind it.|They left the conversation with good manners intact.|I wonder what kinds of contest stories they most enjoy hearing.''')
add('contest_report_next','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_LookingForwardToNextContest','A reporter looks forward to the players next contest.','''soft_smile~We have somebody looking forward to the next round already. Friendly pressure.|A returning observer could notice how the performance develops.|Nice to have someone cheering for another attempt.|That makes another entry sound a little less lonely.|Encouragement can be a good thing to carry into practice.|Our next performance has acquired an interested audience in advance.|We have been assigned a future. Fortunately, it sounds rather pleasant.|A chance to try a different approach with someone watching our progress.|A kind expectation can feel like a little lamp ahead.|It is lovely to leave people curious about what comes next.|I would enjoy hearing what they notice the next time.''')

add('gym_randall_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_RandallPostBadge','Randall sees a Gym Leader as someone who keeps training through wins and losses.','''soft_smile~A Leader keeps learning too. The Badge does not graduate your brain.|Continuing after either outcome is a sensible definition of serious practice.|Win or lose, keep doing the work. Fair.|I like that the losing days count as part of it.|A good routine matters on the plain days between big matches.|The title is apparently a promise to remain a student.|Leadership comes with an endless supply of lessons. How inconvenient.|Every result can tell you what needs work next.|Commitment shows in returning after both pride and disappointment.|A title looks best with the work that keeps it earned.|I would be curious which loss taught him the most.''')
add('gym_parker_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_ParkerPostBadge','Parker says training became harder after the player beat the Gym Leader.','''flustered~Our win gave everyone homework. Sorry to their tired practice shoes.|A defeat prompting the whole Gym to revise its training is understandable.|Harder work can help. Rest still matters.|I hope tougher does not mean nobody gets to breathe.|Good training needs fuel and recovery as well as effort.|Our victory has apparently rewritten the staff's afternoon schedule.|We have become the reason somebody groans at another practice round.|They have identified a need to improve. Now the method matters.|Growth should leave them stronger, not simply worn down.|A challenge can sharpen standards without losing good judgment.|I would ask what changed in their actual practice.''')
add('gym_george_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_GeorgePostBadge','George plans to keep training at Gyms and become a Leader.','''soft_smile~A future Leader with plenty of practice planned. Good shoes, George.|Training across Gyms could broaden the experience behind that ambition.|Keep learning. Look after the partners getting you there.|It is nice hearing a goal with real work attached.|A steady plan can carry a big dream a long way.|An aspiring Leader has chosen the long road of earning the title.|A promising ambition, provided the training survives the announcement.|Learning from different Gyms gives him more approaches to compare.|A distant goal becomes closer through ordinary returns to practice.|That kind of confidence looks better with patience beneath it.|I wonder which Leader first made him want the job.''')
add('gym_berke_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_BerkePostBadge','Berke credits the players father with making Petalburg trainers tougher.','''soft_smile~Dad has apparently upgraded the whole town's stubbornness. That sounds familiar.|A Gym Leader's methods can affect the wider training community.|Good leadership should make the people around it better.|That must be a nice thing to hear about your dad.|It sounds like his work is helping people beyond the Gym.|A father's reputation has traveled well beyond the family table.|The town has acquired a noticeably stronger work ethic.|A change in leadership seems to have improved the local training system.|Good care for a place can show in the people who live there.|A strong reputation is especially lovely when it helps others grow.|I would ask what he does differently that people have noticed.''')
add('gym_mary_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_MaryPostBadge','Mary wants trainers and Pokemon to become soul mates.','''soft_smile~A partner who knows all your tiny odd habits and still stays. That sounds lovely.|Trust built through repeated care is a meaningful goal for training.|Know your partner. Let them know they can count on you.|That is a gentle reason to work so hard together.|The everyday care is where that closeness has room to grow.|A grand ambition measured in understanding rather than trophies.|I would settle for a partner who forgives my awkward silences.|The strongest coordination starts with paying attention to each other.|A bond like that is grown through many small choices.|Being understood is a very beautiful kind of companionship.|I would love to hear when she first felt that closeness.''')
add('gym_alexia_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_AlexiaPostBadge','Alexia asks whether the player has tried Surf.','''soft_smile~Surf is a big new kind of going places. I would start near shore.|A useful new way to explore, with sensible preparation for open water.|Check the route before heading far from shore.|The first quiet stretch across water must feel wonderful.|A dry bag for the supplies would be very welcome.|A simple question with an entire coastline of possibilities behind it.|Walking's aquatic rival has entered the conversation.|I would like to see how the partner handles the crossing.|New water can make familiar land seem different.|A new route is exciting, even before choosing the destination.|I would ask which crossing she enjoyed trying first.''')
add('gym_jody_badge','PetalburgCity_Gym_Text_JodyPostBadge','Jody says a trainers feelings for their Pokemon decide victory beyond strength.','''soft_smile~Caring matters. Knowing what our friends need helps us help them shine.|Affection can support good decisions, especially when paired with preparation.|Trust matters. So does understanding the match.|A partner who feels safe with you has something important.|Care is in the little choices made before the big moment.|A contest of strength is also a conversation between partners.|Feelings are more useful when they remember to pay attention.|A strong partnership improves how the whole team works together.|Love shows itself in what we ask and what we notice.|Confidence sits better on a partner who knows they are valued.|I would be curious which match made that belief feel true.''')
add('wattson_endeavor','MauvilleCity_Gym_Text_WattsonGoForthAndEndeavor','Wattson heartily encourages the player to go forth and keep trying.','''laughing~That laugh could power the first three steps. Off we endeavor!|A concise encouragement with a rather impressive delivery.|Keep going. Do the work. Good advice.|That is difficult to hear without smiling a little.|A hearty send-off can put some energy back in the day.|Our departure has been blessed with a laugh of excellent carrying power.|Endeavor has rarely sounded so cheerfully unavoidable.|A good moment to take what we learned and actually use it.|A generous voice can send us onward a little lighter.|An energetic farewell suits him wonderfully.|I think his laugh will stay with us past the door.''')
add('fortree_last_badge','SootopolisCity_Gym_1F_Text_GoGetFortreeBadge','A Gym adviser directs the player to Fortree for their last required Hoenn Badge.','''surprised~One Badge left, and it has a town attached. That makes the next step clear.|A precise remaining requirement is helpful for planning the route.|Fortree next, then. Get the team ready.|Being that close must make the last trip feel different.|One more stop deserves the same good preparation as the first.|Our next chapter has been given a wonderfully unambiguous address.|The long list has become one last errand with considerable pressure.|A clear target helps us focus the team's next preparations.|A nearly finished path still deserves careful steps.|The final missing piece has a very specific place to find it.|I would check the route and give everyone a good rest before setting out.''')

add('favor_thanks','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_ThankYouForLastTime','The Favor Lady quietly thanks the player for their previous help.','''soft_smile~She remembered. A little thank-you can travel quite a long way.|The earlier help appears to have left a pleasant impression.|Good to know the help mattered to her.|That quiet thank-you feels very sincere.|It is nice when a small kindness is remembered.|A modest line that gives our earlier visit a lovely echo.|Gratitude does not always need a grand entrance.|An earlier favor has clearly stayed in her memory.|Some thanks arrive softly and remain all the same.|A gentle acknowledgment is sometimes the nicest reception.|I like seeing that she still remembers our earlier visit.''')
add('favor_goodbye','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_IsThatSoGoodbye','The Favor Lady ends the conversation after the player declines sharing.','''soft_smile~A quiet goodbye. We can leave the offer there for today.|The request has ended with a clear refusal accepted.|We owe her nothing. We can head on.|She sounded disappointed, but she let us go.|Sharing should stay something we choose.|Our encounter concludes with remarkably little ceremony.|A farewell can be brief without needing to become hostile.|No exchange today. That keeps the arrangement simple.|A small parting can be left gentle.|We can accept the goodbye without making it awkward.|I would give her a friendly farewell in return.''')
add('favor_unsuitable','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_IllTryToCherishIt','The Favor Lady politely accepts a gift that does not meet her desired quality.','''soft_smile~It was not quite what she imagined, but she is trying to be kind about it.|A mismatch in expectations, met with an effort at appreciation.|Not the right fit. Still decent of her to thank us.|That awkward little pause says a lot.|A gift can miss the taste and still deserve thanks.|A delicate acceptance balanced between honesty and good manners.|Her gratitude has arrived wearing slightly uncomfortable shoes.|Useful feedback, though she is being careful with the wording.|Good intentions and the right gift do not always arrive together.|She is trying to be gracious about a less than perfect match.|I would remember the preference more carefully next time.''')
add('favor_cherish','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_IWillCherishThis','The Favor Lady warmly appreciates a gift matching her preferred quality.','''soft_smile~We found something that fits her little dream. That feels good.|The choice appears to match her preference quite well.|A good fit for her. Glad she likes it.|That soft reaction makes the gift feel special.|It is lovely when something chosen actually makes the other person happy.|A modest offering has found precisely the right admirer.|The gift has received a very gentle lifetime appointment.|A successful match between the request and the item.|A small thing can shine when it meets the right person's eye.|The right choice looks lovely in someone else's hands.|I would remember how her face changed when she saw it.''')
add('favor_return_gift','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_IllGiveYouThisInReturn','The Favor Lady offers a return gift in appreciation of the players present.','''soft_smile~One gift became two happy people. A good little exchange.|Reciprocity was not required, but the gesture is thoughtful.|Kind of her. We should thank her too.|That is a sweet way to share her happiness.|A return gift carries a little of the original kindness with it.|Our gift has come back to us in an entirely different form.|The exchange has developed an unexpectedly generous second half.|Both people have found something to appreciate. Nice result.|Kindness can travel back without losing where it began.|A gracious response to a gift she clearly enjoyed.|I like that she wants us to treasure something as well.''')
add('favor_prize_space','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_YouDontHaveSpaceForIt','The Favor Lady keeps a return gift until the players bag has room.','''soft_smile~The gift is ready; our bag is still arguing with its own contents.|The exchange can wait until there is safe storage for the item.|Make room first. She will still have it.|I appreciate the patient way she put that.|A little sorting will let us accept it properly.|Her generosity has briefly run into the very solid wall of our inventory.|Our bag has managed to decline a gift on our behalf.|A small storage change should finish the exchange.|The thought is already kind, even while the gift waits.|An organized bag would complete this gracious little moment.|We can return when we can actually carry what she offers.''')
add('quiz_waiting','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_WaitingToTakeYourQuiz','The Quiz Lady is waiting for someone to answer the players quiz.','''soft_smile~Our question is out there waiting to surprise somebody. Tiny suspense.|We have supplied the puzzle; another participant supplies the test.|Let someone else have a try. We made it.|I would be curious how someone else reads our question.|It is fun to share a little challenge and wait for the reaction.|Our words are awaiting their first brave reader.|The quiz has entered the socially awkward waiting-for-company phase.|A new participant will show whether the question works as intended.|A question changes a little when another mind receives it.|Now we get to discover how our idea comes across.|I would love to hear what the first challenger says.''')
add('quiz_decline','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_HowBoringBye','The Quiz Lady calls the players refusal boring and says goodbye.','''annoyed~Declining a quiz is allowed. It does not require a tiny boredom verdict.|A refusal is not evidence that the person lacks interest in everything.|We passed. That is all she needed to hear.|That felt a little sharp for a simple no.|A guest can decline without spoiling the whole day.|Our departure has received a review nobody requested.|Boring has its charms. Chiefly fewer unsolicited quizzes.|That reaction is not making the next invitation more appealing.|A quiet answer need not become a small judgment.|One declined activity does not make a person dull.|I would rather she stayed curious about what people actually enjoy.''')
add('quiz_quit','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_TakeTheQuizAnotherTime','The Quiz Lady accepts leaving an ongoing quiz for another time.','''soft_smile~The question can wait. My thinking parts appreciate the extension.|A pause is reasonable when the player no longer wants to continue.|Another time. We can stop here.|I appreciate being able to leave it unfinished.|A fresh mind might enjoy it more later.|Our unanswered question has been given permission to remain mysterious.|An incomplete quiz is a tolerable addition to the universe.|Stopping is better than guessing just to escape the process.|Some questions can rest without needing an immediate answer.|A graceful pause preserves the possibility of enjoying it later.|I would return when we actually feel like puzzling over it.''')
add('quiz_create_decline','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_MaybeNextTime','The Quiz Lady accepts declining to create a new quiz.','''soft_smile~No new riddle today. The world has enough things wondering already.|We can devise a question when we have a suitable idea.|No quiz to write now. We can return.|I would rather think of something than force it.|A good idea can come along when we are doing something else.|The unwritten puzzle has been spared a hurried and unfortunate birth.|An idea is allowed to miss its appointment.|We can develop a better question before starting the next attempt.|A little time gives an idea room to arrive.|A future attempt can be more thoughtfully put together.|I like that she left the choice open for later.''')
add('quiz_prize_full','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_YourBagIsFilledUp','The Quiz Lady holds a won prize until the players bag has room.','''laughing~We answered the quiz, but the bag failed the practical exam.|The prize is earned. Capacity is the remaining issue.|Make room. The win is already ours.|A little delay after getting it right is still manageable.|We can clear a spot before collecting the reward.|An intellectual triumph has met a logistical footnote.|Our brain had room for the answer. Our bag had other plans.|A quick storage adjustment will finish what the answer started.|The reward can wait without taking away the pleased feeling.|A successful answer deserves a properly arranged place for the prize.|I would remember to collect it once the bag is sorted.''')
add('contest_block_thanks','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_ThankForPokeblock','The Contest Lady remembers and thanks the player for an earlier Pokeblock.','''soft_smile~A tiny snack made a lasting impression. Excellent work, tiny snack.|The gift has remained memorable enough to prompt another thanks.|Glad it helped. Kind of her to remember.|That makes the small gift feel rather special.|Food shared with someone's partner can mean a lot.|A bite-sized favor has earned a rather pleasant return appearance.|The cube was small. Apparently the gratitude was well supplied.|Nice to know our contribution was not forgotten.|Some little offerings leave a warm place behind them.|A thoughtful thank-you is a lovely thing to receive twice.|I would ask how her Pokemon has been doing since then.''')
add('contest_block_refusal','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_WhatACheapskate','The Contest Lady insults the player after they decline giving a Pokeblock.','''annoyed~A snack is a gift, not an admission fee for being treated nicely.|Refusing a request does not establish anything about a person's generosity.|We said no. Insulting us does not change it.|That makes me less comfortable with the whole request.|A treat freely shared is lovely. Guilt is a poor ingredient.|A rejected request has become an unflattering character review.|The price of politeness appears to be exactly one Pokeblock.|That is an ineffective way to encourage future cooperation.|An offered kindness cannot be pulled out of someone by shame.|Calling someone cheap is a very expensive way to lose goodwill.|I would rather she asked kindly and accepted the answer.''')
add('contest_no_case','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_DontHaveAPokeblockCase','The Contest Lady realizes the player lacks a Pokeblock Case and postpones her request.','''soft_smile~Hard to share a snack from a case we do not have. Mystery solved.|The request depends on equipment we currently lack.|No case, no block to give. She understands.|That is a relief after such an eager request.|We cannot share what we are not carrying.|The proposed gift exchange has encountered an entirely empty premise.|Our nonexistent snack container has provided a convincing excuse.|The required container is missing. We can revisit this later.|The moment can pass without forcing something that is not there.|A practical little detail has settled the conversation.|I would find out where to get the case before worrying about the request.''')
add('contest_no_change','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_NoChangeThanks','The Contest Lady thanks the player despite seeing no change from the Pokeblock.','''soft_smile~No obvious change, but a kind try still got a thank-you.|A visible effect was not observed. The gratitude remains appropriate.|Did not help as hoped. We still tried.|I like that she thanked us even when it was not what she expected.|Not every treat changes something. It can still be a gift.|A modest experiment has produced no dramatic result and some decent manners.|The snack has declined to perform a miracle.|Useful to notice a result without inventing an improvement.|A small offering need not prove itself to have been kind.|An honest reaction with a gracious finish.|I would remember that result when choosing another block.''')
add('contest_improved','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_ReallyImprovedThanks','The Contest Lady is delighted that the Pokeblock improved her partners condition.','''soft_smile~A happy Pokemon and a delighted trainer. That little cube did well.|A positive response and a reported condition improvement. Promising result.|Glad the partner liked it. That matters first.|That delight makes the choice feel worth it.|A treat that suits its eater is a very satisfying success.|The tiny gift has received an excellent review from both parties.|One cube, two delighted customers. Remarkable efficiency.|We found a good match. Useful to remember what worked.|A little shared food has brought a bright moment.|The right choice has made the whole pair look happier.|I would like to see the Pokemon's reaction rather than just hear the result.''')
add('contest_ready','LilycoveCity_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_ReadyToEnterContests','The Contest Lady feels ready to enter contests and hopes for the players support.','''soft_smile~We might recognize a familiar face in the contest. I can supply cheers.|It would be interesting to see how the preparation carries into an entry.|Glad they feel ready. We can cheer fairly.|I would like to see them enjoy the performance.|I will be happy to wish them well when they enter.|Our small contribution has become an invitation to witness the debut.|A future contestant has acquired one slightly awkward cheer squad.|A good chance to see the results of their preparation.|It is lovely to be asked to share a hopeful moment.|A friendly face in the audience can make the room feel kinder.|I would watch for them next time we visit a contest.''')

add('profile_cancel','ProfileMan_Text_NotIntoItRightNow','The profile collector accepts the player canceling creation for now.','''soft_smile~Our grand introduction can wait until the words stop hiding.|A profile can be composed when the player actually wants to make one.|No rush. We can leave it for now.|It is hard to sum yourself up on demand.|A few good words are better than something hurried.|The unfinished portrait has been permitted a little more thought.|We have declined the terrifying task of explaining ourselves briefly.|A little preparation could make choosing the phrases easier.|Some thoughts need a quieter moment to find their shape.|A profile can wait until it feels like it actually fits.|I would rather hear a sincere introduction than a rushed one.''')
add('profile_praise','ProfileMan_Text_FantasticProfile','The collector enthusiastically praises the players finished profile.','''flustered~That is a lot of applause for a few words. The words are standing taller.|A very positive response to a concise self-description.|Glad he likes it. That was generous.|Oh. That much praise would make me look at my shoes.|It is nice to have a little effort greeted so warmly.|Our miniature autobiography has received a magnificently expansive review.|Four words have apparently captured the entire collector.|A compact description with a very successful first audience.|A little of ourselves was offered and met kindly.|It seems the profile made exactly the impression he hoped for.|I would love to know which part caught his attention first.''')
add('profile_decline','ProfileMan_Text_ImagineYouWouldHaveWonderfulProfile','The collector imagines the player would have a wonderful profile after refusal.','''soft_smile~A flattering guess. I hope our imaginary profile has excellent punctuation.|A kind impression, even without the requested information.|Nice of him. We still do not have to share.|That was a gentle way to sound disappointed.|A compliment is easier to accept when it leaves us a choice.|Our unwritten profile has already attracted a favorable review.|The imagined version of us is doing exceptionally well today.|He has left the idea open without needing an immediate result.|A kind guess can be left as a little gift.|A gracious compliment with room to keep our privacy.|I like that his curiosity stayed friendly after the refusal.''')
add('profile_unchanged','ProfileMan_Text_LikeProfileWayItIs','The collector approves the players decision to keep their existing profile.','''soft_smile~If the words still fit, they can stay. No need to redecorate ourself today.|An unchanged description is reasonable if it remains accurate.|Keep it if it works. Nothing wrong with that.|I like not having to invent a new version of myself.|Something good does not need replacing just because we returned.|The revised edition has been canceled in favor of the beloved original.|Our existing self has passed another inspection.|No redesign needed if the current version still does its job.|Some words keep their place because they remain true.|A familiar profile can still be the right fit.|I would be interested in what finally makes someone change those words.''')
add('fan_recommendation','LilycoveCity_PokemonTrainerFanClub_Text_YouShouldMeetTrainer','A fan recommends meeting their favorite trainer and predicts the player will become a fan.','''soft_smile~A very confident introduction for someone who is not even here.|A personal recommendation is a good reason to listen, if not proof.|We can meet them and decide for ourselves.|It is sweet when someone wants to share a favorite person.|They clearly enjoy telling people what they admire.|An absent trainer has acquired an extremely loyal advance publicist.|Our admiration has apparently been scheduled without consulting us.|I would like to hear what the trainer actually does well.|Another person's delight can be an invitation to look closer.|An introduction can be flattering without deciding our taste for us.|I would ask what moment made them become a fan.''')
add('fan_interview_done','LilycoveCity_PokemonTrainerFanClub_Text_ThankYouIllShareThisInfo','A fan thanks the player and plans to discuss the information with other fans.','''soft_smile~Our little answer is about to become a whole club conversation.|Shared information is useful when it is passed along accurately.|Hope they keep the details straight when repeating it.|I would be a little nervous hearing my words had an audience.|A good conversation can give people plenty to talk about.|Our account is leaving the room with an eager distribution network.|We have just become the source of an unusually enthusiastic discussion.|Useful to distinguish what we actually said from the extra excitement.|Words travel farther when they find people who care.|A lively discussion will go better if the quotation stays accurate.|I would be curious which part they decide is most interesting.''')
add('fan_tv_special','LilycoveCity_PokemonTrainerFanClub_HopeYouCatchTVSpecial','A fan recommends an upcoming television special about a trainer.','''soft_smile~A favorite trainer gets a whole special. That fan will be very punctual.|A focused program may provide more detail than the usual brief reports.|We can keep an eye out. Thanks for the tip.|They sound excited to have something new to watch.|An excuse to sit down together can be nice.|A forthcoming broadcast has acquired an enthusiastic personal endorsement.|The fan club's evening has apparently planned itself.|I would be interested in seeing how the trainer approaches a match.|It is kind to share something they are looking forward to.|A well made special might show what all the enthusiasm is about.|I would watch for the small details the fans mention afterward.''')
add('berry_mix_instruction','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_MakePokeblocksDifferentBerries','A receptionist explains using different berries together to make Pokeblocks.','''soft_smile~Everyone brings a different berry. A little snack committee with actual variety.|Different ingredients contribute to the mixture. Coordination helps.|Check what everyone brought before starting.|I like a shared task where each person adds something.|Variety in the berries helps make the batch worth sharing.|Our culinary ensemble has been instructed to avoid identical contributions.|A group project where bringing the same thing is actually a problem.|Agreeing on inputs first should save a wasted batch.|Different small gifts can become something good together.|A little variety makes a much more interesting blend.|I would ask who likes which berry before everyone chooses.''')
add('ferry_unavailable','LilycoveCity_Harbor_Text_FerryUnavailable','A harbor attendant explains that the ferry service is unavailable.','''sad~No sailing yet. The harbor is still doing its waiting impression.|The route is unavailable for now. We should plan around that.|No ferry today. Use another route.|That is disappointing, but at least we know.|We should keep our supplies for the route we can actually take.|Our maritime departure has been postponed before it found a vessel.|The ship we seek is currently a very confident absence.|We need an available route, rather than an optimistic schedule.|Waiting water does not promise a boat today.|A changed itinerary is easier once the facts are clear.|I would ask what is keeping the service from starting.''')
add('sailor_waiting','LilycoveCity_Harbor_Text_SailorFerryUnavailable','A sailor impatiently awaits the ferry being built in Slateport.','''soft_smile~A sailor without a boat has a lot of land to be impatient on.|Construction can take time, especially for something carrying many people.|Better finished properly than launched too soon.|Waiting must feel especially long when you want to be useful.|The builders probably want a good ship as much as the sailors do.|A maritime career is temporarily at the mercy of a very terrestrial timetable.|A sailor stranded by carpentry has understandably developed opinions.|A ferry needs careful work. Pressure cannot replace a sound hull.|There is work waiting on both sides of the unfinished thing.|Patience is difficult when the job you want depends on someone else's.|I would like to hear what their first day aboard will be like.''')
add('rest_decline','Route111_OldLadysRestStop_Text_DontNeedToBeShy','An old lady responds to a refused rest offer by reassuring the player.','''soft_smile~A kind invitation. We can still decide whether our feet are ready to stop.|A hospitable offer, even if our choice is not caused by shyness.|Good of her. We can rest when we need it.|I know what it is like to hesitate over accepting care.|A little rest can be a gift, with nothing to earn first.|Our host has mistaken a refusal for bashfulness, very kindly.|Hospitality has made a gentle second attempt at reaching us.|A useful stop to remember when the walk catches up with us.|We can receive the kindness even if we keep walking.|Her welcome is warmer than any awkwardness around the answer.|I think she genuinely enjoys having travelers stop in.''')
add('cable_car_decline','Route112_CableCarStation_Text_RideAnotherTime','A Cable Car attendant politely accepts a declined ride.','''soft_smile~The mountain will still be tall when we are ready to ride.|A later trip remains possible. We can choose a better moment.|Another time. Nothing lost by waiting.|I appreciate a simple farewell after a simple choice.|We can check our plans before heading uphill.|Our ascent has been deferred with excellent professional courtesy.|The cable car has survived our refusal to be elevated.|A postponed ride is easy enough to arrange later.|There is no need to hurry toward every high place.|A polite invitation makes a return trip feel welcome.|I would like to come back when we can enjoy the whole view.''')
add('lanette_boxes','Route114_LanettesHouse_Text_OrganizeYourBoxes','Lanette recommends organizing storage boxes so their Pokemon are easy to identify.','''soft_smile~A label beats opening every box and saying oh, there you are.|Good organization reduces the effort of finding the right Pokemon.|Know where everyone is. Saves time and mistakes.|I like being able to find a familiar partner without guessing.|A little sorting now makes later choices much easier.|The inventor has offered the gloriously practical advice of naming where things go.|Chaos has been politely asked to acquire labels.|Clear organization makes a good system much easier to use.|A place is kinder when its residents are not lost in the arrangement.|An orderly collection should still be easy to understand at a glance.|I would ask how she organizes her own boxes.''')
add('castform_explanation','Route119_WeatherInstitute_2F_Text_PokemonChangesWithWeather','A researcher explains the gifted Pokemon changes form with weather and welcomes the player taking it.','''surprised~A new friend with a very personal weather forecast. That is wonderful.|Weather-dependent form changes are a remarkable trait to observe.|Interesting partner. We should learn what each change means.|I would like to see how it behaves in different weather.|We should make sure the new partner is comfortable wherever we go.|A generous gift, with the sky providing an unusually active wardrobe.|The little creature has outsourced part of its appearance to the clouds.|A living response to conditions. I have so many questions.|A companion whose shape listens to the sky. Lovely.|Its look changes with the weather? That is an extraordinary collection.|I would love to compare those forms without making it uncomfortable.''')
add('weather_limits','Route119_WeatherInstitute_2F_Text_ChangingWeatherRidiculous','A researcher with years of rain study dismisses freely changing weather as unrealistic.','''soft_smile~Years of rain have made them suspicious of anyone claiming a sky remote.|Long observation is a good reason to question sweeping claims of control.|Weather is bigger than one person's wishes. Fair point.|They sound like someone who has watched a lot of clouds refuse instructions.|People who depend on weather know it rarely keeps convenient hours.|A seasoned witness has declined to let ambition issue orders to the sky.|The clouds have consistently failed to attend our planning meetings.|A system that large deserves more respect than a casual promise.|Knowing rain well may teach a person how much remains beyond reach.|A strong claim should come with more than confidence and a dramatic pose.|I would ask which years of study most shaped that opinion.''')

add('treasure_bag','Route124_DivingTreasureHuntersHouse_Text_BagFull','The treasure hunter cannot complete a shard trade because the players bag is full.','''soft_smile~A treasure trade needs somewhere for the new treasure to go.|Capacity is the obstacle, rather than the value of the shard.|Make room before trading. Keep the shard safe.|A little rearranging should make this easier.|We can keep what we need and clear a little space.|The treasure has reached the border of a very crowded bag.|Our pockets have defeated another perfectly reasonable exchange.|Check the outgoing and incoming items before making the trade.|Leave a small empty place for what comes next.|A successful exchange needs more than a good choice of treasure.|I would sort the bag before asking him to start again.''')
add('treasure_decline','Route124_DivingTreasureHuntersHouse_Text_ComeBackIfYouChangeMind','The treasure hunter is disappointed by a declined trade but welcomes a return.','''soft_smile~He wanted the treasure, but he is letting us keep the decision.|We can compare the options before committing to an exchange.|Our shard, our call. Come back if it suits us.|I am glad the disappointment stayed friendly.|It is fine to hold on to something until we know.|The proposed bargain has retired gracefully to a possible future scene.|The treasure hunter has survived not acquiring a treasure.|No need to exchange a useful item without a clear reason.|An offered trade can remain an invitation.|A little hesitation is allowed when choosing what to keep.|I would ask about the options before making up my mind.''')
add('treasure_no_shards','Route124_DivingTreasureHuntersHouse_Text_YouHaventGotAnyShards','The treasure hunter asks the player to bring any shards found later.','''soft_smile~A little shard now has a destination. We should remember this house.|A useful contact if we recover any suitable fragments.|Keep an eye out. No need to risk a dive for his enthusiasm.|It is nice knowing a small find could matter to somebody.|We can bring one by if we happen to find it.|Our wandering has acquired a minor treasure-hunting subplot.|The missing treasure has been requested with impressive optimism.|We should learn what the shards look like before searching.|Small things washed aside can still find a welcome.|A little fragment may be just what completes somebody's collection.|I would like to know what first made him start collecting them.''')
add('safari_advice_done','SafariZone_South_Text_EnjoyTheRestOfYourAdventure','A Safari attendant wishes the player enjoyment after their assistance.','''soft_smile~A helpful stop and a cheerful send-off. Back to the little wild surprises.|Good advice is most useful when we take time to apply it.|All set. Keep watching where we walk.|That makes continuing feel rather welcoming.|A good outing leaves time to enjoy the place itself.|Our brief consultation concludes with a fine wish for the expedition.|We have official permission to remain pleasantly curious.|Time to try what we learned and see what happens.|The path still has room for something unexpected.|An encouraging farewell suits a place full of new sights.|I would slow down enough to notice the rest of the adventure.''')
add('safari_help_open','SafariZone_South_Text_GoodLuck','A Safari attendant wishes luck and remains available for help.','''soft_smile~Luck AND someone to ask. That is a good combination for wandering.|It is useful to know where help is available.|Good. We know where to come if needed.|I appreciate being told it is all right to ask.|A friendly person nearby makes a big unfamiliar place easier.|A reliable supporting character has made themself available.|Our exploration now has a sensible fallback plan.|We can try things without pretending we already know everything.|Help nearby can make a quiet path feel less lonely.|An approachable attendant is an excellent feature of any outing.|I would remember the way back here before heading farther.''')
add('safari_repeat_welcome','Route121_SafariZoneEntrance_Text_ComeInAndEnjoy','A Safari entrance attendant welcomes a returning visitor inside.','''soft_smile~Back to the Safari! This time the surprises may recognize our shoes.|A return visit may reveal things we missed on the first circuit.|Ready to go. Keep the rules in mind.|I like having another chance to notice something quietly.|A familiar entrance can still lead to a very different day.|Our expedition receives its second and pleasantly uncomplicated invitation.|The wilderness has graciously allowed another performance of our curiosity.|We can try a different route from the last visit.|A known path is not the same as a finished discovery.|A return visit gives us room to look beyond the first impression.|I would choose one thing to watch more closely this time.''')
add('safari_rules','Route121_SafariZoneEntrance_Text_FirstTimeInfo','The entrance attendant explains thirty Safari Balls and a five-hundred-step visit limit.','''surprised~Thirty throws, five hundred steps. My wandering has become arithmetic.|Limited balls and steps make deliberate route choices useful.|Count on limits. Do not waste the start rushing.|I would like to pause and look before choosing a direction.|We should make the visit count without turning it into a hurry.|An adventure with a very specific allowance of footwear and ambition.|At last, my meandering has been assigned an official ceiling.|A little route planning will help make good use of both limits.|A measured walk can still hold a surprising amount of wonder.|We can spend the visit on what we actually want to see.|I would watch where the first few paths lead before using the whole allowance.''')
add('dock_delivery','SlateportCity_SternsShipyard_1F_Text_MeetDockDeliverToStern','Dock introduces himself as the ferry designer and asks the player to find Stern for delivery.','''soft_smile~We found the boat designer, but the parcel still needs its actual person.|Dock has clarified the recipient and why he cannot take the delivery.|Find Stern. Deliver it to the right hands.|He seems busy enough without being the wrong recipient too.|A parcel for someone deserves the care of reaching that person.|Our delivery story has acquired a designer, though not yet its ending.|The parcel has arrived near its destination in the most inconvenient sense.|A clear handoff matters. We need the person responsible for the goods.|An errand is not finished merely because the building looks right.|A useful introduction, even if the delivery needs another stop.|I would ask where Stern was last seen before we search.''')
add('dock_where_stern','SlateportCity_SternsShipyard_1F_Text_CouldYouFindStern','Dock repeats his request to locate Stern and deliver the parcel.','''soft_smile~Still looking for Captain Stern. The parcel has become our quiet co-explorer.|The task remains unchanged: locate Stern and complete the handoff.|Find Stern first. Keep the parcel with us.|I hope someone nearby knows where he went.|We can finish the errand once we find the person waiting for it.|The missing captain continues to be the central complication of delivery.|Stern has developed an impressive talent for being elsewhere.|A new lead would be more useful than checking the same room.|The person we seek has left a small ripple of questions.|Best find a fresh direction before retracing every step.|I would ask one of the other workers whether Stern mentioned a stop.''')
add('blender_company','BerryBlender_Text_MakePokeblocksUsingBerryBlender','An old man offers to make Pokeblocks together using the blender.','''soft_smile~A shared batch sounds nice. The berries get dizzy and we get company.|An agreeable chance to compare timing and share the result.|Good offer. We can join if we have what we need.|Making something together sounds easier than finding small talk.|I enjoy an invitation that comes with a bowl of ingredients.|A cordial partnership, proposed over a machine full of future treats.|A practical reason to stand near someone without needing a grand conversation.|I would enjoy seeing how an experienced participant uses the blender.|A little work shared can turn strangers into company.|An inviting little project with something pleasant at the end.|I would ask how long he has been making them here.''')
add('blender_no_spares','BerryBlender_Text_DontHaveAnyBerriesNoneToSpare','An old man regrets that neither the player nor he has spare berries for blending.','''sad~An empty-berry standoff. Neither side has brought the round little solution.|The shared activity is blocked by a missing ingredient on both sides.|No berries today. We can try another time.|It is kind that he thought of sharing his own.|We can return with enough for a batch and a little to spare.|An amiable collaboration has found itself entirely without raw materials.|A tragic shortage at the very first stage of snack creation.|We know the missing input. That makes the next visit simple.|The offer to share still counts, even when the hands are empty.|A gracious thought, despite a rather bare supply situation.|I would bring a few different berries when we return.''')
add('blender_gift_plan','BerryBlender_Text_UseItToMakePokeblocksTogether','An old man gives a berry with plans to blend together.','''soft_smile~A berry with a social invitation attached. Very efficient friendliness.|A small gift has removed the obstacle to participating together.|Kind of him. We can make the batch now.|That makes joining in feel much less awkward.|An ingredient shared is a lovely way to welcome someone.|Our partnership has been funded by a single generous berry.|He has solved the snack problem and the stranger problem together.|A useful contribution that gets the little project moving.|A shared beginning can be as small as one berry.|A thoughtful gift that also gives us something pleasant to do.|I would like to see him enjoy the batch he helped us join.''')
add('route111_gift_decline','Route111_Text_DontWantThis','A Route 111 tutor accepts declining their gift and remains available.','''soft_smile~Not for us right now. They left the offer open kindly.|A decision we can revisit if the gift becomes useful.|We can pass. No need to take everything offered.|I like that a no did not make the conversation difficult.|A thoughtful offer stays thoughtful when it leaves us a choice.|The gift has been returned to the realm of future possibilities.|An offered thing has survived the horror of not immediately being wanted.|We can return once we know how we would use it.|Something can be offered kindly and still stay where it is.|A gracious response to a perfectly reasonable choice.|I would remember the invitation if our plans change.''')
add('route111_gift_full','Route111_Text_DontHaveAnyRoom','A Route 111 tutor keeps a gift until the players bag has room.','''soft_smile~The gift can wait. Our bag needs to stop collecting every possible possibility.|A little storage space is all that prevents the handoff.|Clear a spot before we return. They will hold it.|That makes the delay feel quite easy.|It is kind to keep the gift safe for us.|Our full bag has created a remarkably minor cliffhanger.|The bag has once again confused possession with preparedness.|A little sorting will make accepting the item straightforward.|There is no need to hurry when the gift is safely waiting.|A quick edit to what we carry would finish this exchange.|I appreciate knowing we can return without losing the offer.''')

add('wallace_sky_pillar','CaveOfOrigin_B1F_Text_WellHeadToSkyPillar','Wallace recognizes Sky Pillar as the next destination and urgently departs; control returns without a warp.','''surprised~Sky Pillar, then. We have a direction, and Wallace is already moving.|A concrete destination is useful. We should follow with proper preparation.|We know where to go. Stay sharp on the way.|He sounded relieved to have an answer, even with the urgency.|We should check everyone can manage the trip before following.|The uncertainty has finally become a place we can actually reach.|At least the urgent question now has an address.|A clear next step. We should plan the fastest safe way there.|A named path is easier to follow than a room full of worry.|A little preparation will help us arrive able to do something.|I would keep that destination clear while we work out the route.''')
add('space_maxie_warning','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_MaxieDontInterfere','Maxie orders the player away during a standalone field interaction.','''annoyed~That is a very loud way to say he would prefer no witnesses.|His wish to avoid interference does not make the situation acceptable.|We are staying aware. He does not give us orders.|I do not like how certain he sounds that we should step aside.|The people here have more reason to feel safe than he does.|A command with considerable confidence and very little moral authority.|He has mistaken volume for a convincing argument.|I would rather understand what is happening than follow his instruction.|Fearful obedience would make this easier for exactly the wrong person.|An unpleasant demand does not become reasonable because he delivers it firmly.|I would watch what he is trying to keep us away from.''')
add('space_tabitha_warning','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_WellTakeCareOfYou','Tabitha threatens the player for interfering with the attempt to take rocket fuel.','''annoyed~They came to steal fuel and now complain about interruptions. Incredible manners.|The threat confirms they expect resistance to the theft.|Stay ready. Threats do not make stealing acceptable.|He sounds far too pleased about threatening people.|The staff should not have to put up with this.|A thief has discovered that other people object to the theft.|An astonishing grievance from someone busy taking what is not his.|Rocket fuel is dangerous enough without someone making threats around it.|His irritation says nothing about who belongs here.|A remarkably entitled way to justify a very poor visit.|I would keep an eye on both him and the fuel they want.''')
add('space_prepare','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_StevenHurryGetReadyQuickly','Steven urges preparation after the player declines immediately joining the battle.','''surprised~Quick, but properly quick. A ready team beats a team still fumbling its bag.|Preparation should be efficient without skipping the necessary checks.|Heal up. Choose the team. Then go back.|The urgency is real. I would still take one steady breath.|We can get everyone ready without wasting the moment.|A brief intermission, with the danger refusing to leave the room.|Time to become prepared at a slightly unreasonable speed.|Check the essentials first. That saves more time than rushing blindly.|A steady hand can move quickly without becoming careless.|Get the practical things right before stepping back in.|I would make a short plan and follow it in order.''')
add('space_steven_thanks','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_StevenThankYouComeSeeMeAtHome','Steven thanks the player after the crisis and invites a visit to his Mossdeep home.','''soft_smile~That was tense. I am glad he remembered to include directions with the thank-you.|A kind invitation after a dangerous effort. The immediate threat is over.|Glad everyone got through it. We can visit when ready.|He sounds relieved. I think I am too.|A quiet visit sounds better than another emergency.|A dramatic rescue concludes with gratitude and a useful correction of address.|A tense afternoon has been converted into a slightly awkward house call.|First make sure everyone is all right. Then a visit sounds good.|The quiet after danger makes an ordinary invitation feel welcome.|A gracious thank-you, complete with the information needed to accept it.|I would like to hear how the staff are doing before we head out.''')
add('space_volcano_plan','MossdeepCity_SpaceCenter_2F_Text_MaxieUseFuelToEruptVolcano','Maxie reveals a plan to throw rocket fuel into Mt Chimney to cause an eruption; this exchange ends before the separate readiness interaction.','''annoyed~That mountain is not his rubbish bin. People live with what it does.|Deliberately provoking an eruption could endanger far more than his target.|We stop that plan. Fuel stays out of the volcano.|The way he sounds pleased about it makes me cold.|There are lives around that mountain, not just land on his plan.|He has mistaken devastation for an impressive ending.|A spectacularly cruel use for something meant to reach the sky.|Rocket fuel does not belong anywhere near an uncontrolled eruption.|A mountain holds more lives than he is choosing to see.|Calling it savage does not make the damage admirable.|I would focus on keeping that fuel away from his plan.''')
add('daycare_egg_decline','Route117_Text_IllKeepIt','The Day-Care Man accepts keeping an Egg the player declined.','''soft_smile~He will keep it. Better than taking on a little life before we are ready.|A responsible choice depends on willingness as well as available space.|He has it safely. We made the choice.|I am glad the Egg is staying with someone who will care for it.|A new responsibility should be welcomed, not accepted from pressure.|The smallest possible new chapter has been left in capable hands.|An Egg is a rather important thing to accept merely to be polite.|The caretaker can handle it while we keep our present commitments.|Saying no can still leave something small safely held.|A kind hand is more important than a hurried change of owner.|I would want to know it will be cared for, and he seems willing.''')
add('daycare_egg_care','Route117_Text_TakeGoodCareOfIt','The Day-Care Man entrusts an Egg to the player and asks for good care.','''soft_smile~A whole little future to carry gently. We can do that.|A responsibility accepted. Gentle handling and patience are appropriate.|We will keep it safe. Careful with the carrying.|It feels rather special being trusted with something so small.|A new arrival begins with a warm, safe place.|A brief instruction with an entire promise inside it.|Our company has increased by one very quiet possibility.|We should keep the Egg protected during the rest of the journey.|Something not yet seen is already worth our care.|A delicate new addition deserves thoughtful arrangements.|I wonder who we will get to meet when it is ready.''')
add('daycare_single_well','Route117_Text_YourMonIsDoingFine','The Day-Care Man reports that the players one boarded Pokemon is doing well; only terminal when no mail follow-up prints.','''soft_smile~Our friend is doing fine. That is the news I came to hear.|A reassuring report from the person watching our partner.|Good. Nice to know they are all right.|That would take a little weight off my mind.|It is lovely to hear a partner is comfortable while away.|A modest update with an unusually comforting conclusion.|No crisis, no dramatic development. Excellent news.|A straightforward check-in can be very useful.|Knowing they are cared for makes the distance feel smaller.|A simple good report is quite enough to brighten the visit.|I would like to hear which part of the day they seem to enjoy.''')
add('daycare_mail','Route117_Text_FriendlyWithOtherTrainersMon','The Day-Care Man reports friendship with another trainers Pokemon and possible mail.','''surprised~Our friend made a friend AND maybe got mail. A very social little stay.|An interesting social observation. The possible mail adds a curious detail.|Good they have company. We should check the mail.|That is a sweet surprise to hear while visiting.|I am glad they found someone pleasant to spend time with.|Our partner's offscreen adventures have acquired both company and correspondence.|They have been away briefly and already have a better social life.|I would like to know how the little delivery happened.|Friendship found a way to leave a small sign behind.|A new acquaintance and a little note. Quite a charming stay.|I would ask whether the two Pokemon spend much time together.''')

add('sludge_gift','DewfordTown_Hall_Text_GiveYouSludgeBomb','An enthusiast gives a Sludge Bomb TM after belittling the players unfamiliarity.','''flustered~A useful gift wrapped in a very unnecessary little insult.|Sharing the move was generous. The disparaging explanation was less helpful.|Thanks for the TM. Could have skipped calling us pitiful.|I wish the gift had come without making someone feel foolish.|Offering to teach is kinder than mocking what someone does not know.|A generous gesture has unfortunately retained its rather sharp packaging.|The present is welcome. Its accompanying opinion can stay here.|A new technique is useful information, regardless of that delivery.|Knowledge is nicer when it is offered without shame.|A good gift with an unfortunate choice of wrapping words.|I would rather hear what they like about the actual move.''')
add('scarf_gift','DewfordTown_House2_Text_WantYouToHaveSilkScarf','A fashion enthusiast delightedly gives the player a Silk Scarf.','''soft_smile~We admired so convincingly that the scarf came home with us.|A generous response to a perceived shared appreciation.|Kind gift. Keep it clean on the road.|They are so pleased to have someone share their taste.|It is lovely when giving something makes the giver this happy.|The admirer has been promoted to the owner in one dazzling speech.|Our eyes have apparently signed a very fashionable agreement.|A soft accessory is a pleasantly simple piece of equipment.|A little delight has become something we can carry.|Now that is an enthusiast who enjoys sharing the look.|I would like to see their face when we put it to good use.''')
add('soda_reward','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_TakeTheseSodaPopBottles','Mr Sea rewards defeating all house trainers with six Soda Pops.','''laughing~Six bottles! Our hot streak has been thoroughly rehydrated.|A substantial reward for completing the whole series of matches.|Earned those. Check the team and take a breather.|He sounds as happy as if he won something himself.|Cold drinks after that effort are a thoughtful reward.|The fiery competition concludes with an impressively fizzy curtain call.|We have converted victory into a portable collection of bubbles.|Enough refreshment to make the next break a good one.|It is nice when effort is met with such obvious delight.|An enthusiastic reward, offered in a very generous quantity.|I think he enjoyed watching us as much as we enjoyed winning.''')
add('trick_next','Route110_TrickHouseEnd_Text_MakeNewTricksToStumpYou','The Trick Master takes a solved puzzle as a challenge to devise a harder installment.','''laughing~We solved it so hard that he is already building revenge furniture.|A successful solver can be useful feedback for a puzzle designer.|Good challenge. We will see what he makes next.|I was not smirking. I think this is just my relieved face.|He seems to enjoy making the next challenge as much as this one.|Defeat has been reclassified as an advertisement for the sequel.|The wounded genius has taken refuge in future inconveniences.|I would love to see which part of the design he changes.|A finished riddle can plant the seed of another one.|That is a rather dramatic way to invite a return visit.|I would ask which solution surprised him most.''')
add('trick_journey','Route110_TrickHouseEnd_Text_LeavingOnJourney','The Trick Master leaves to discover new tricks and hopes for a future entertaining reunion.','''soft_smile~Off to find more tricks. I hope his travels are full of excellent little puzzles.|Seeking new experiences could broaden the challenges he designs.|Good journey to him. Hope he finds what he is looking for.|That goodbye sounds softer than his usual challenges.|Travel can give a busy mind new things to enjoy.|The trickster has left his own house to become the audience for once.|The world is about to receive an unusually demanding puzzle enthusiast.|New places are excellent sources of unexpected design ideas.|May the road offer him a surprise he could not build himself.|A journey of inspiration sounds like a fine next chapter for him.|I would like to hear what delighted him when he eventually returns.''')
add('macho_brace_gift','Route111_WinstrateFamilysHouse_Text_LikeYouToHaveMachoBrace','Victoria gives the familys Macho Brace after the player defeats them all.','''soft_smile~We won the family challenge and a piece of the family workout equipment.|A gracious reward that shares something important to their training.|Kind of them. Winning does not mean we stop learning.|They sound proud of the challenge even after losing.|A useful gift from people who clearly care about their practice.|The defeated household has responded with an admirably practical tribute.|A family heirloom, apparently designed to make exercise more inconvenient.|Interesting to try the equipment behind their training routine.|A loss can still leave room for respect and generosity.|A thoughtful gift, even with that little doubt about whether we need it.|I would ask how each family member uses it in practice.''')
add('glass_complete','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_IveFinishedGlassItem','The glassworker hands over the finished ash-made item on successful collection.','''soft_smile~Our dusty walking has become an actual thing! A very satisfying transformation.|A fine example of collected material finding a useful finished form.|Good work. Keep the new glass secure.|It is lovely seeing the result after all that gathering.|There is something satisfying about taking home work made from what we brought.|The humble ash has completed its surprising transformation.|Our footsteps have acquired a tangible and much less dusty ending.|I would like to look at the finish and how the shape was made.|Something gathered softly from the road has taken a new form.|A finished piece makes the whole collecting trip feel well chosen.|I would ask how long that particular piece took to shape.''')
add('flower_planting','Route104_PrettyPetalFlowerShop_Text_BerriesExplanation','The shop owner explains replanting berries and asks for help filling the world with flowers.','''soft_smile~One berry back in the ground. A tiny thank-you that grows its own flowers.|Replanting keeps the cycle going while allowing a harvest.|Take some, plant some. Good habit.|I like a dream that lets us help in small ways.|Leaving a berry to grow means there will be more to share.|A beautiful ambition built from very ordinary acts of planting.|A grand dream with an unusually sensible first instruction.|A system that replenishes its own materials deserves care.|A little fruit returned can become a patch of beauty later.|A flower-filled world begins with remembering the next planting.|I would enjoy finding a blooming tree we planted on an earlier visit.''')
add('flower_happiness','Route104_PrettyPetalFlowerShop_Text_FlowersBringHappiness','The shop owner says flowers bring happiness.','''soft_smile~They do. Even a tiny flower can make a whole patch look pleased.|A small visible change can make a familiar place more pleasant.|A bit of color helps a place feel cared for.|A little flower by a window can change a room.|A few flowers on the table make an ordinary day feel special.|A brief argument for beauty, supported by a great many windowsills.|They are remarkably effective for something that says so little.|A small growing thing can improve a space without much machinery.|They ask little of a passerby and still offer something lovely.|Color, shape, and a little life. A very good combination.|I like noticing which flowers people choose to keep near them.''')

add('tv_checking','MauvilleCity_Text_BeenCheckingOutTV','A Mauville man ends his television explanation with a casual question about watching TVs.','''soft_smile~The televisions are getting checked on very thoroughly around here.|He seems interested in whether we noticed the local broadcasts.|We have seen a few. He is keen on them.|I wonder which program he wanted us to notice.|A good show can give people something pleasant to talk about.|Our viewing habits have acquired an unusually persistent local correspondent.|The television has apparently become a civic obligation.|I would ask which program he thinks is worth watching.|A familiar screen can hold a little shared window for a town.|His enthusiasm makes me curious what he has been seeing.|I would like to know which broadcast first caught his attention.''')
add('slateport_on_tv','SlateportCity_Text_AmIOnTV','A bystander near Sterns interview excitedly wonders whether they are on television.','''laughing~The camera found one interview and several people hoping to be the background.|The field of view may include bystanders. Recognition is another matter.|Maybe. Do not crowd the interview.|I would suddenly forget what to do with my hands.|They seem pleased just to be part of the moment.|An extra has discovered the possibility of an entirely accidental debut.|The fame has not arrived yet, but the waving appears ready.|It depends where the camera is pointed. Quite a practical question.|A small chance of being seen can make a person wonderfully lively.|Background presence can still make someone's whole afternoon.|I love noticing people who suddenly realize the camera is there.''')
add('fossil_handoff','RustboroCity_DevonCorp_2F_Text_HandedFossilToResearcher','A Devon researcher eagerly accepts a fossil to begin their work.','''surprised~Our old little fossil has found somebody very excited to give it a future.|A promising specimen has reached someone equipped to investigate it.|Good. Let the researcher get to work.|They sound so pleased to have something new to study.|We brought it to someone who seems ready to care for the task.|A piece of the distant past has entered an unexpectedly energetic appointment.|The fossil has traded a quiet bag for a very busy desk.|I would love to see the equipment they use for this work.|An old shape may be ready to tell us something new.|That enthusiasm makes the handoff feel very well placed.|I would ask what they examine first before we leave them to it.''')
add('contest_prize_wait','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_ComeBackForPrizeLater','A contest receptionist holds a prize for later collection.','''soft_smile~Our prize has a safe place to wait. The victory is already ours.|The collection is deferred, rather than the result being lost.|We can come back. Remember to collect it.|It is reassuring that they will keep it for us.|A reward can wait until we are ready to carry it.|The award ceremony has encountered a very manageable scheduling note.|Our winnings have been granted temporary accommodation.|Good to know the prize can be collected after we sort things out.|The pleased feeling need not wait beside the physical prize.|A patient little arrangement for something already earned.|I would make a point of returning before the day gets away from us.''')
add('gmode_wireless','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_NoWirelessAdapterInGMode','The receptionist explains that G-Mode needs a cable rather than a wireless adapter.','''flustered~The mode and the connector disagree. At least they told us which one to change.|A specific compatibility requirement. We need the appropriate connection or mode.|Wrong setup. Change the mode or use the cable.|That is much easier than guessing why it will not start.|A little clear guidance saves everyone another frustrating try.|Our grand linked entrance has been delayed by an exceptionally small connector.|The invisible connection has failed to satisfy a very visible rule.|Clear fault report, clear alternatives. I appreciate that.|Some doors open only when the little pieces match.|An awkward mismatch with a pleasantly straightforward explanation.|I would check the setup before asking them to try again.''')
add('minigame_farewell','MossdeepCity_GameCorner_1F_Text_ComeAgain','A minigame attendant accepts a canceled game and invites another visit.','''soft_smile~No game this time. We can save our heroic button presses for later.|A canceled attempt need not make the next visit awkward.|Another time. We can leave it there.|I like a place that lets you change your mind.|An outing can still be good without doing every activity.|Our planned diversion concludes before requiring a score.|We have narrowly escaped having our coordination quantified.|A later try might suit us better. Simple enough.|An open invitation can be left gently for another day.|A pleasant goodbye makes returning easy.|I would come back when everyone actually wants to play.''')
add('pokemon_jump_rules','MossdeepCity_GameCorner_1F_Text_PokemonJumpInfo','A minigame attendant explains small grounded Pokemon skipping Vine Whip together in time.','''laughing~Tiny jumpers, one rope, many chances to discover who was daydreaming.|Size and movement restrictions make sense for a synchronized jumping game.|Choose someone suited to jumping. Watch the timing.|That sounds fun once everyone finds the same rhythm.|A little coordination can turn a simple game into a lovely group activity.|A tiny ensemble of jumpers faces one extremely punctual vine.|A very small contest with excellent opportunities for public mistiming.|Shared timing is the interesting challenge, beyond just getting airborne.|A little leap feels different when everyone rises together.|Small participants deserve a game made for their own scale.|I would watch a round to see how they keep one another in time.''')
add('dodrio_rules','MossdeepCity_GameCorner_1F_Text_DodrioBerryPickingInfo','An attendant explains directing Dodrios three heads to catch falling berries.','''laughing~Three hungry heads and one person trying to organize lunch. Good luck.|A three-direction response task should be an interesting coordination test.|Watch the berries. Give each head a clear direction.|I would probably apologize to the head I forgot.|Three heads at snack time sounds like a very busy kitchen.|A culinary drama in which all three leading roles share one body.|An entire argument about berries, now available as a game.|Three controlled inputs and moving targets. I would enjoy trying that.|Each head gets its own little moment to notice and reach.|Three competing appetites are a remarkable challenge to coordinate.|I would love to see how differently the heads react to a missed berry.''')
add('minigame_redirect','MossdeepCity_GameCorner_1F_Text_TalkToOldManToPlay','A helper directs prospective minigame players to the old man beside them.','''soft_smile~We asked the explanation person. The starting person is one person over.|A helpful distinction between information and arranging the game.|Talk to the old man next. Clear enough.|That was a kind way to point us in the right direction.|A little guidance can save a lot of standing around.|Our inquiry has been transferred a very manageable distance.|An impressively short referral through the local bureaucracy.|The instructions and the controls have different caretakers.|One small direction can make an unfamiliar place easier.|A clear next step is always a useful finishing touch.|I would thank the helper before speaking to the old man.''')
add('minigame_adapter','MossdeepCity_GameCorner_1F_Text_AdapterNotConnected','The minigame attendant says the wireless adapter must be connected before returning.','''flustered~The wireless part still needs a piece attached. That is a sneaky detail.|The required adapter must be present before the connection can work.|Connect the adapter first. Then try again.|At least there is a clear reason it would not start.|We can sort the equipment before asking for another try.|Our wireless adventure has encountered a decidedly physical missing piece.|The connection has declined to transcend the need for its own hardware.|A missing component is a nice straightforward problem to identify.|A little gap in the arrangement can stop the whole thing.|One small accessory has turned out to be the essential one.|I would check everything is fitted before we return.''')

add('designer_dex_incomplete','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_ShowMeCompletedDex','The game designer encourages continuing the Pokedex and returning when complete; terminal on incomplete-Dex branch.','''soft_smile~A big project, and someone interested in seeing the finish. That helps.|A long observational task benefits from patience and consistent records.|Keep at it. No need to finish everything today.|I like having someone who wants to see the work when it is ready.|A little progress on an ordinary day still counts.|The unfinished collection has acquired an encouraging future reviewer.|Completion can take its time. The world has many small moving subjects.|A good record grows through careful observations, not just a rushed count.|A patient curiosity can carry us a very long way.|A complete collection begins with noticing each individual well.|I would enjoy showing them the discoveries that surprised us most.''')
add('daycare_boarded','Route117_PokemonDayCare_Text_WellRaiseYourMon','The Day-Care Woman accepts a Pokemon for care; terminal only when this fills the second care slot.','''soft_smile~Our friend has a place to stay. We should remember to come check on them.|The care arrangement is in place. A later visit will let us assess the stay.|They have our partner. We come back for them.|I hope the stay gives them something pleasant to do.|It is good to know someone will be watching over them.|A brief separation begins with a clear promise of a return.|Our partner has acquired temporary accommodation and a very important reservation.|We should keep track of the arrangement and plan the return visit.|Leaving gently includes remembering to return.|A little stay should end with a proper, cheerful reunion.|I would like to hear how our partner settles in.''')
add('old_trainer_spectator','SootopolisCity_MysteryEventsHouse_1F_Text_OnlyAmusementWatchingBattles','A former traveling trainer now takes pleasure in watching younger trainers battle.','''soft_smile~He has plenty of old adventures and still enjoys seeing new ones happen.|Watching can remain rewarding after a long career of participating.|He earned a seat. Hope he sees a good match.|I would like to hear one of his own travel stories.|Sharing the excitement can still make for a lovely afternoon.|The old adventurer has become an appreciative audience for the next generation.|He has found the comfortable side of competitive battling.|Experience must make certain little choices especially interesting to watch.|A journey can change shape without losing all its joy.|A good spectator brings a lifetime of appreciation to the room.|I wonder what he notices now that he missed as a young trainer.''')
add('old_trainer_decline','SootopolisCity_MysteryEventsHouse_1F_Text_YouWontBattle','The older host is disappointed when the player declines a visiting-trainer battle.','''soft_smile~He wanted a good match. We can still choose when we are ready.|The spectator's disappointment does not obligate a participant.|No battle today. He can be disappointed without us changing it.|I feel a little bad, but I would not want to be pushed.|A match should be something both trainers actually want.|Our host has lost the afternoon's hoped-for entertainment.|The audience's wishes have encountered the competitor's right to rest.|A voluntary match works better than one entered just to appease someone.|A gentle refusal can coexist with a little disappointment.|We can be gracious without turning the answer into a yes.|I would like him to know we appreciated the invitation.''')
